UPDATE goals SET description = 'The travellers press on through Northern Dunland, keeping the high slopes of the Misty Mountains to their right hand. Having left the old beggar Saruman muttering by the wayside, the company finds the air fresher and the road open before them. They begin to draw away from the steep foothills, riding over wide, grassy swells of land that show little sign of recent war. It is a quiet leg of the journey, marked only by the steady rhythm of hooves and the grey peaks watching silently from the east.' WHERE distance = 2629 * 1.60934;

-- Goal: Draw farther and farther from the mountains and foothills (Distance: 2674)
UPDATE goals SET description = 'The travellers follow the road through Dunland as it bends westward, carrying them steadily away from the dark roots of the Misty Mountains. As the rocky foothills recede into the grey distance, the landscape flattens, guiding the company towards the low-lying wetlands that wait to the north. The ancient marshes of the Swanfleet lie ahead, marking the boundary where the wild lands will soon give way to the ruins of Eregion on their homeward journey.' WHERE distance = 2674 * 1.60934;

-- Goal: Marshes of the Swanfleet lie to the north (Distance: 2719)
UPDATE goals SET description = 'The company rides northwards through the deserted lands of Eregion, leaving the Misty Mountains on their right hand. To their left, the Marshes of the Swanfleet spread out in a haze, marking the junction where the Glanduin meets the loud-flowing Hoarwell. These fenlands are a sombre sight, echoing with the cries of river-birds, but offering no easy passage for the travellers. The hobbits keep to the firmer ground east of the wetlands, their hearts lightening as each mile brings them closer to the Last Homely House.' WHERE distance = 2719 * 1.60934;

-- Goal: Can see mists above the fens of the Swanfleet delta (Distance: 2759)
UPDATE goals SET description = 'The returning travellers look out over the confluence of the Glanduin and the Greyflood, watching the pale mists coil above the fens of the Swanfleet. Although the Nîn-in-Eilph seems quiet now, the hobbits recall tales of the great hosts of swans that once inhabited this vast, watery delta. The company rides along the borders of the marshland, their path taking them steadily closer to the ancient realm of Eregion and the road to Rivendell. The grey haze over the pools obscures the horizon, serving as a bleak yet peaceful marker on their homeward journey.' WHERE distance = 2759 * 1.60934;

-- Goal: Reach the ruins of Ost-en-Edhil (Distance: 2809)
UPDATE goals SET description = 'The Company walks amidst the crumbled foundations of Ost-en-Edhil, where the Gwaith-i-Mírdain once crafted rings of power in the shadow of the Misty Mountains. Legolas pauses to listen to the stones, hearing them lament the fair folk who vanished from Eregion long ago. The eerie silence of the land unsettles the other travellers, for only the cry of birds breaks the stillness of this desolate country. As they continue east along the old road, the three peaks of Moria rise like jagged teeth against the grey sky.' WHERE distance = 2809 * 1.60934;

-- Goal: Continue east on Moria-road. Mountains of Moria rise ahead (Distance: 2839)
UPDATE goals SET description = 'The company follows the ancient stones of the Moria-road through the desolate yet fair lands of Hollin, drawing ever closer to the roots of the Misty Mountains. To the east, the three great peaks of the Mountains of Moria—Caradhras, Celebdil, and Fanuidhol—pierce the sky, their snowy caps gleaming innocently in the sunlight. This sight stirs dark memories for the hobbits, who recall the bitter snows of the Redhorn Pass and the terror of the wargs that once hunted them in this very wild. Yet now the air is peaceful, and the empty land holds no echo of the Shadow, offering only the quiet solitude of Eregion.' WHERE distance = 2839 * 1.60934;

